From a7991b865b9dc6143873f58af6f13b5067735123 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (Aefinity lab session)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:11:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] lab: CIS-1 VNNI kernel, row-parallel integer decode,
 TPM-attested receipts, repack scale fix

aegis-core
- cis_vnni.rs: AVX-512 VNNI (zmm) and AVX-VNNI (ymm) ternary matvec for CIS-1,
  byte-identical to cis::ternary_matvec_i8 (tests/cis_vnni_equivalence.rs);
  CPUID/XGETBV probe (no_std); falls back to cis_avx2 then scalar; same 2-bit
  container and traffic. 1-row default; 4-row-blocked variant behind
  set_force_r4 (measured slower on first silicon, kept for iron A/B).
- cis_infer.rs: tmv_dispatch routes x86_64 through cis_vnni; under `parallel`
  the CIS matvecs and the LM head split output rows across the existing pool
  (bit-identical by construction: rows are independent integer dots).
- benches/vnni_vs_avx2.rs: same-process interleaved 3-arm A/B with a
  DRAM-streaming mode (rotates distinct weight copies).

aegis-linux
- examples/cis_decode_timed.rs: cis_decode plus decode-loop timing, CPU named
  from CPUID, env=vm flagged, digest printed per repeat (Rule A: ratios only).

aegis-uefi
- attest.rs (AEGIS-ATTEST v0): measure MODEL.SAF/EMBED.BIN/VOCAB.BIN
  (+RECEIPT.TXT) into TPM PCR 12 and the CIS-1 witness chain + verdict into
  PCR 13 via EFI_TCG2_PROTOCOL (EV_IPL events, replayable from the log);
  TPM2_PCR_Read of PCR 4/12/13; TCG2 event-log excerpt; TPM2_CreatePrimary
  (ECC P-256) + TPM2_Quote over PCR 4,12,13 with qualifyingData =
  SHA-256(RECEIPT.TXT), resend on TPM_RC_RETRY; ATTEST.TXT report.
- verifier.rs: factor replay()/render_receipt() so the unikernel can MINT a
  witness v1 receipt (MINT.TXT: max_new + prompt) with the same arithmetic
  the Linux cis_witness uses; Verdict carries chain/cis_digest/steps.
- main.rs: TPM measurement after STAGE 5, mint mode, ATTEST.TXT, whole-file
  writer. No TPM = logged finding, behaviour otherwise unchanged.
- tpm2min (path dep): no_std, no-alloc, forbid(unsafe_code), zero-dependency
  TPM 2.0 wire format (Startup, PCR_Read, PCR_Extend, CreatePrimary, Quote,
  FlushContext); quotes verified against swtpm with tpm2-tools, OpenSSL and an
  independent parser.

aegis-forge
- repack_ternary.py: --scale-convention {auto,reciprocal,multiply}. The
  shipped reciprocal convention is right for transformers BitLinear
  (Falcon-E, HF1BitLLM) and WRONG for Microsoft's offline-quantized packed
  BitNet checkpoint (AutoBitLinear multiplies); auto sniffs
  quantization_config.quant_method == "bitnet". With it the repack of
  microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T reproduces CIS_DECODE digest cab11400d737ac4a.

Lab evidence (QEMU/OVMF + swtpm, correctness only; VM timing ratios only) is
recorded outside this repository in the session's lab logs.
